        -:   23:/*`restrict` is spelled bare, which is C99 syntax.
        -:   24:
        -:   25:It is carried only by read_fasta()'s block buffer, which this file allocates
        -:   26:itself and reaches through nothing but that pointer and the ones derived from
        -:   27:it. Every other pointer here is perl's: an SV, AV or HV, or the PV inside one,
        -:   28:which the perl API may alias behind the code's back -- in write_fasta() a
        -:   29:defline and its sequence can be COW copies of the one buffer -- so the
        -:   30:qualifier would be a false promise. perl is built with -fno-strict-aliasing,
        -:   31:where `restrict` is the only disambiguation there is, but it earns nothing even
        -:   32:on the buffer: the loop over it stores only through memchr() and sv_catpvn(),
        -:   33:which are opaque calls the compiler must assume write anywhere. The generated
        -:   34:code for this file was byte-identical with and without it (gcc -O2 -std=gnu99,
        -:   35:2026-09-30), so the one annotation records the contract rather than buying
        -:   36:speed.
        -:   37:
        -:   38:Makefile.PL probes for a C99 flag but cannot always find one. MSVC accepts the
        -:   39:keyword only under /std:c11 or later and otherwise spells it __restrict, older
        -:   40:gcc spells it __restrict__, and a strict C89 compiler has no equivalent. Map it
        -:   41:where a spelling exists and define it away where none does -- the same block as
        -:   42:~/Scripts/stats/LikeR.xs. It sits below every #include so that it cannot
        -:   43:rewrite a parameter named `restrict` inside a system header.*/
        -:   44:#if !defined(__cplusplus) && !defined(restrict)
        -:   45:#  if defined(_MSC_VER)
        -:   46:#    define restrict __restrict
        -:   47:#  elif !defined(__STDC_VERSION__) || __STDC_VERSION__ < 199901L
        -:   48:#    if defined(__GNUC__)
        -:   49:#      define restrict __restrict__
        -:   50:#    else
        -:   51:#      define restrict /*no spelling available; annotation only*/
        -:   52:#    endif
        -:   53:#  endif
        -:   54:#endif
